 "name": "Redline",
 "_about": "After cauliflowermossgrape's Redline app (MIT): G20-style rev bar with shift lights, big gear, shift point with the cold-engine guard, and every upshift graded. The scale runs to the redline's thousand + 1000; shift point = redline - the Shift point setting. Fitted (Nov 5 2026 grid photo) to the part of the HUD the driver sees, x 120..605, y 100..378, with a 6 px margin: lights and the rpm readout on top, the bar and its scale, then the gear in the middle with SHIFT beside it, speed, oil and coolant on the left, and the shift point, last shift, grade and cold note stacked on the right. The bottom-left x 150..355, y 314..378 is left to BMW's own speed and speed-limit sign, which it keeps drawing over ours in Comfort.",
